  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"2026.9.4\"\n  # upstream refs: https://github.com/jdx/mise/blob/main/scripts/build-tarball.sh & https://github.com/jdx/mise/blob/main/scripts/build-tarball.ps1\n  base_features: native-tls,rustls-native-roots,vfox/vendored-lua\n  extra_features: ${{ \",aws-lc-rs\" if target_platform == \"linux-armv7l\" else \"\" }}\n  self_update_msg: \"This version of mise was installed from conda-forge, a community-maintained channel of Conda packages. Use your Conda package manager (`conda`, `mamba`, `pixi` etc.) to update mise.\"\n\npackage:\n  name: mise\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/jdx/mise/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 745a677234f0482e9ee6abaf897e220a2d8375f8a7868e8fb50833dedcb0c5fc\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  script:\n    env:\n      AWS_LC_SYS_CMAKE_BUILDER: ${{ \"1\" if win else \"0\" }} # force CMake builder for `aws-lc-sys` native C/C++ code on Windows\n      CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_LTO: \"thin\" # `rustc-LLVM` runs out of memory with `fat` LTO\n      CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_STRIP: symbols\n      OPENSSL_NO_VENDOR: \"1\"\n      # instruct `cc` crate to use clang-cl natively to compile build-time tools intended to be run on the host when cross-compiling from `win_64`\n      # (fixes compilation of `zstd-sys`)\n      AR_x86_64_pc_windows_msvc: llvm-lib\n      CC_x86_64_pc_windows_msvc: clang-cl\n      CXX_x86_64_pc_windows_msvc: clang-cl\n    content:\n      # NOTE: we have to set LIBCLANG_PATH for bindgen to find libclang\n      # cf. https://github.com/conda-forge/clangdev-feedstock/issues/373 & https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-bindgen/issues/918\n      - if: unix\n        then:\n          - export LIBCLANG_PATH=\"$BUILD_PREFIX\"/lib\n          - cargo auditable install --path=. --root=\"$PREFIX\" --no-track --locked --bins --no-default-features --features=${{ base_features }}${{ extra_features }}\n          # write custom `mise self-update` message\n          - mkdir -p \"$PREFIX\"/lib\n          - echo 'message = \"${{ self_update_msg }}\"' > \"$PREFIX\"/lib/mise-self-update-instructions.toml\n          # copy manpage\n          - mkdir -p \"$PREFIX\"/share/man/man1\n          - cp man/man1/mise.1 \"$PREFIX\"/share/man/man1/mise.1\n          # generate shell completions\n          - if: build_platform == host_platform\n            then:\n              - mkdir -p \"$PREFIX\"/share/bash-completion/completions \"$PREFIX\"/share/fish/vendor_completions.d \"$PREFIX\"/share/zsh/site-functions\n              - '\"$PREFIX\"/bin/mise completion bash > \"$PREFIX\"/share/bash-completion/completions/mise'\n              - '\"$PREFIX\"/bin/mise completion fish > \"$PREFIX\"/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/mise.fish'\n              - '\"$PREFIX\"/bin/mise completion zsh  > \"$PREFIX\"/share/zsh/site-functions/_mise'\n      - if: win\n        then:\n          # bindgen expects libclang.dll; conda-forge only provides versioned DLLs on Windows\n          - powershell -Command \"cp (gci $env:BUILD_PREFIX\\Library\\bin\\libclang-*.dll)[0] $env:BUILD_PREFIX\\Library\\bin\\libclang.dll\"\n          - set \"LIBCLANG_PATH=%BUILD_PREFIX%\\Library\\bin\"\n          - cargo auditable install --path=. --root=\"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\" --no-track --locked --bins --no-default-features --features=${{ base_features }}${{ extra_features }}\n          - cargo auditable install --path=crates\\mise-shim --root=\"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\" --no-track --locked --bins\n          # write custom `mise self-update` message\n          - if not exist \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\lib mkdir \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\lib\n          - echo message = \"${{ self_update_msg }}\"> \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\lib\\mise-self-update-instructions.toml\n          # copy manpage\n          - if not exist \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\share\\man\\man1 mkdir \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\share\\man\\man1\n          - powershell -Command \"Copy-Item -Path 'man/man1/mise.1' -Destination '%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\\share\\man\\man1\\mise.1'\"\n          # generate shell completions\n          - if: build_platform == host_platform\n            then:\n              - if not exist \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\share\\bash-completion\\completions mkdir \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\share\\bash-completion\\completions\n              - if not exist \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\share\\fish\\vendor_completions.d   mkdir \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\share\\fish\\vendor_completions.d\n              - if not exist \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\share\\zsh\\site-functions          mkdir \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\\share\\zsh\\site-functions\n              - '\"%LIBRARY_BIN%\"\\mise.exe completion bash > \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\\share\\bash-completion\\completions\\mise\"'\n              - '\"%LIBRARY_BIN%\"\\mise.exe completion fish > \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\\share\\fish\\vendor_completions.d\\mise.fish\"'\n              - '\"%LIBRARY_BIN%\"\\mise.exe completion zsh  > \"%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\\share\\zsh\\site-functions\\_mise\"'\n      - cargo-bundle-licenses --format=yaml --output=./THIRDPARTY.yml\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('rust') }}\n    - cargo-auditable\n    - cargo-bundle-licenses\n    - clang\n    - cmake\n    - libclang\n    - make\n    - ninja\n    - pkg-config\n  host:\n    - if: linux\n      then: openssl\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      env:\n        MISE_NO_CONFIG: 1\n        MISE_OFFLINE: 1\n      content:\n        - mise help\n        - mise version\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - mise\n        - if: win\n          then: mise-shim\n      files:\n        - if: unix\n          then:\n            - lib/mise-self-update-instructions.toml\n            - share/man/man1/mise.1\n            - if: build_platform == host_platform\n              then:\n                - share/bash-completion/completions/mise\n                - share/fish/vendor_completions.d/mise.fish\n                - share/zsh/site-functions/_mise\n        - if: win\n          then:\n            - Library/lib/mise-self-update-instructions.toml\n            - Library/share/man/man1/mise.1\n            - if: build_platform == host_platform\n              then:\n                - Library/share/bash-completion/completions/mise\n                - Library/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/mise.fish\n                - Library/share/zsh/site-functions/_mise\n      strict: true\n\nabout:\n  summary: mise manages dev tools, env vars, and runs tasks.\n  description: |\n    `mise` (mise-en-place) is a unified CLI tool designed to simplify and manage local development environments.\n    It acts as a polyglot tool version manager, installing and seamlessly switching between versions of various\n    development tools (replacing utilities like `asdf`, `nvm`, and `pyenv`). Additionally, it functions as an\n    environment variable manager that dynamically loads project-specific env vars based on your current directory\n    (replacing `direnv`), and serves as a built-in task runner to define and execute project workflows as a modern\n    alternative to `make` or `npm` scripts.\n  license: MIT\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - THIRDPARTY.yml\n  homepage: https://mise.jdx.dev/\n  repository: https://github.com/jdx/mise\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - salim-b\n",
